 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Ya'qub: no plate; geometric for «فالله خير حافظا وهو أرحم الراحمين», coins for the returned price. Nothing on the denied measure (63:7-9). 65:12-25 is not glossed. STAGING v4: Ya'qub's dwelling is the desert with tents (12:100: he came from the desert, Al-Muyassar: from the badiya). Ya'qub is only a blue drop labelled Ya'qub, at the right. His sons are a plain group of three men (owner decision: plain figures, never the rejecting crowd; 3 figures = a group, not their number), with one camel for the provisions they brought (65: a camel's load). c1 (63): they come back and walk to their father (63:2), then speak (63:5, 63:10, 63:14); nothing is drawn on the denied measure (63:7-9); a wheat plate for the measure they hope for (63:13). Binyamin is not drawn in this video. c2 (64): Ya'qub answers them (64:1, 64:7, 64:15); a geometric plate for Allah as the best guardian (64:12); the listeners make no gesture and nothing glows on Ya'qub. c3 (65): they go to their camel's load (65:2, they opened their goods), a coins plate for the price returned (65:5-7, both tafsirs), come back and speak to their father (65:8), pointing to the load as they say it (65:12, their own words); a wheat plate for the extra camel load (65:21). The cover shows them asking for their brother (63:10)."
